    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\triangle YOM\\cong\\triangle XOM$ by SSS, so $\\angle YOM=\\angle XOM$. Hence $OM$ bisects $\\angle AOB$.",
      "worked": "In $\\triangle YOM$ and $\\triangle XOM$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nYO&=XO &&\\text{(radii of the circle centred at }O\\text{)}\\\\\nYM&=XM &&\\text{(construction circles have radius }OX=OY\\text{)}\\\\\nOM&=OM &&\\text{(shared side)}\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\triangle YOM\\cong\\triangle XOM$ by SSS congruence. Corresponding angles give $\\angle YOM=\\angle XOM$. Since $Y$ lies on $OB$ and $X$ lies on $OA$, $OM$ bisects $\\angle AOB$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
